# Project Rules — Miniclip

## Overview

Miniclip is a minimal clipboard manager for Linux (Wayland/X11), built with Electron and React. It monitors the system clipboard, persists history (text + images) to a local SQLite database, and provides a compact popup window for searching and restoring previous clipboard entries. It runs as a system-tray application and is distributed as a Snap, .deb, and AppImage.

- **License**: GPL-3.0-only
- **App ID**: `com.miniclip.app`
- **Desktop name / executable**: `miniclip`

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Version |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime | Electron | 44.x |
| UI Framework | React | 18.x |
| Language | TypeScript (strict) | 5.x |
| Build tool | Vite | 5.x |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/postcss`) | 4.x |
| Database | better-sqlite3 (native, synchronous) | 13.x |
| Logging | electron-log | 5.x |
| Packaging | electron-builder | 26.x |
| Linting | ESLint + @typescript-eslint | 8.x / 7.x |

## Project Structure

```
miniclip/
├── electron/                  # Electron main process
│   ├── main.ts                # App lifecycle, IPC handlers, clipboard polling, tray, DB
│   ├── preload.ts             # contextBridge API exposed to renderer
│   └── electron-env.d.ts      # Node/Electron env type augmentations
├── src/                       # Renderer process (React)
│   ├── main.tsx               # Entry point — hash-based routing (#preferences, #about)
│   ├── App.tsx                # Main clipboard history UI
│   ├── Preferences.tsx        # Settings window
│   ├── About.tsx              # About window
│   ├── PinIcon.tsx            # SVG pin icon component
│   ├── index.css              # Tailwind imports, GNOME theme CSS variables, custom utilities
│   ├── vite-env.d.ts          # Global type declarations (ClipboardItem, Window.electronAPI)
│   └── shared/
│       └── settings.ts        # Settings interface + defaults (shared between main & renderer)
├── scripts/
│   ├── build.mjs              # Programmatic electron-builder entry (snap workaround + publish)
│   ├── fix-appimage.mjs       # Pre-pack hook: patches AppImage desktop file version
│   └── update-metainfo.mjs    # Pre-build hook: syncs AppStream metainfo with package.json
├── build/
│   ├── applications/          # .desktop file
│   └── metainfo/              # AppStream appdata XML
├── public/                    # Static assets (icons, tray images)
├── .github/workflows/
│   └── release.yml            # CI: build + publish on tag push
├── electron-builder.json5     # Packaging config (Linux targets: appimage, deb, snap)
├── vite.config.ts             # Vite + electron plugin config
├── tsconfig.json              # TypeScript config (strict, ES2020, react-jsx)
└── .eslintrc.cjs              # ESLint config
```

## Architecture & Key Patterns

### Process Model

- **Main process** (`electron/main.ts`): All system interaction — clipboard polling (500ms interval), SQLite DB, tray, window management, settings (JSON file), IPC handlers.
- **Preload** (`electron/preload.ts`): Exposes typed `window.electronAPI` via `contextBridge`. All renderer↔main communication goes through this.
- **Renderer** (`src/`): Pure React UI. No direct Node/Electron imports. Communicates exclusively through `window.electronAPI`.

### IPC Pattern

- **Events (main → renderer)**: `clipboard-change`, `settings-changed`, `window-hidden` — subscribed via `ipcRenderer.on`, return cleanup functions.
- **Invoke (renderer → main)**: `get-history`, `copy-to-clipboard`, `delete-history-item`, `clear-history`, `toggle-pin`, `hide-window`, `minimize-window`, `close-window`, `get-settings`, `set-settings`, `get-version`, `open-external`.

### Database

- SQLite via `better-sqlite3` (synchronous API).
- DB file: `clipboard_history.db` in `app.getPath('userData')`.
- Table `clipboard_history`: `id`, `content`, `content_type` ('text'|'image'), `original_format`, `created_at`, `hash`, `pinned`, `sort_time`.
- Images stored on disk in `userData/images/`, referenced via custom protocol `miniclip-img://`.
- History trimmed by `maxHistorySize`; pinned items excluded from trimming.

### Settings

- Stored as JSON in user data directory.
- `Settings` interface in `src/shared/settings.ts` — imported by both main and renderer.
- Changes broadcast via `settings-changed` IPC event.

### Routing (Renderer)

- No router library. Hash-based: `#preferences` → Preferences, `#about` → About, default → App.
- Each "page" is a separate BrowserWindow with the appropriate hash.

### Theming

- GNOME-inspired design with CSS custom properties for light/dark themes.
- Theme switches via `prefers-color-scheme` media query.
- Custom Tailwind colors: `gnome-bg`, `gnome-surface`, `gnome-accent`, `gnome-text`, `gnome-text-dim`, `gnome-border`, `gnome-input`.
- Custom utilities: `draggable` / `no-drag` (for Electron window drag regions).

### Single Instance

- Uses `app.requestSingleInstanceLock()`. Second instance with `show` arg focuses existing window.

### Wayland Compatibility

- Global shortcuts NOT registered in-app — users set them via system settings (`miniclip show` CLI).
- On Wayland sessions the app forces the X11 (XWayland) backend via `--ozone-platform=x11` (self-relaunch at the top of `electron/main.ts`; dev flag in `vite.config.ts`). Wayland's core clipboard protocol only serves the focused client, so an unfocused clipboard manager can't read the clipboard reliably without it.

## Commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Start Vite dev server with Electron |
| `npm run build` | Full production build (tsc → vite build → scripts/build.mjs) |
| `npm run build:publish` | Build + publish to GitHub/Snap Store |
| `npm run lint` | ESLint check (ts, tsx — zero warnings allowed) |
| `npm run preview` | Preview production build |

## Coding Conventions

### TypeScript

- **Strict mode**: `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`.
- Target ES2020, module ESNext, bundler module resolution.
- JSX: `react-jsx` (automatic runtime).
- Prefer interfaces for data shapes, types for unions/function signatures.

### React

- Functional components only, hooks-based.
- `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`, `useCallback` — standard hooks.
- No class components, no Redux/external state management.
- Components are in flat `src/` directory (no deep nesting).
- Event handlers named `handle*` (e.g., `handleSelectItem`, `handleDeleteItem`).

### Styling

- Tailwind CSS utility classes exclusively — no CSS modules or styled-components.
- Use GNOME theme color tokens (`text-gnome-text`, `bg-gnome-surface`, etc.) — not raw colors.
- Dark mode handled automatically via CSS variables + `prefers-color-scheme`.

### Electron Main Process

- Use `electron-log` for all logging (not `console.log`).
- All IPC handlers registered in `main.ts` using `ipcMain.handle()`.
- Database operations are synchronous (better-sqlite3 API).
- Wrap DB operations in try/catch, log errors with `log.error()`.
- Global error handlers for `uncaughtException` and `unhandledRejection`.

### File Organization

- Shared types/interfaces between main and renderer go in `src/shared/`.
- Type declarations for the renderer go in `src/vite-env.d.ts`.
- Build scripts go in `scripts/` as ESM (`.mjs`).

## Packaging & Release

- **Targets**: AppImage, .deb, Snap (Linux only — no macOS/Windows).
- **CI**: GitHub Actions, triggered on tag push (`*`).
- **Publishing policy** (in `scripts/build.mjs`):
  - Prerelease versions (containing `-`) → Snap Store `edge` + GitHub pre-release.
  - Release versions → Snap Store `stable` + GitHub release.
  - Override with `SNAP_CHANNEL=<channel>` env var.
- **Snap**: core24 base, strict confinement, LXD builds.
- **Version bumping**: update `package.json` version; `prebuild` hook auto-updates metainfo XML.

## Important Caveats

- **No tests exist** — there is no test framework configured.
- **Linux-only** — no macOS or Windows support.
- **No router** — multi-window hash routing is manual.
- **better-sqlite3 is native** — marked as `external` in Vite config and must be rebuilt for the target Electron version (handled in CI).
- **Snap has special constraints** — desktop file naming, StartupWMClass, environment variables. Read the comments in `electron/main.ts` and `electron-builder.json5` before changing snap-related config.
- **Images use a custom protocol** (`miniclip-img://`) — not base64 data URLs. Protocol handler registered in main process.
